1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,500
Mom counts the little ones every day. Today she stops at five.

2
00:00:02,700 --> 00:00:05,300
A fireboat doesn't just put out fires. It splits waves.

3
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:07,900
The wave has passed, but the road of light is scattered. Which way is home?

4
00:00:08,100 --> 00:00:10,500
Mochi hugs his backpack tight. It grows brighter and brighter.

5
00:00:10,700 --> 00:00:13,300
The closer to home, the brighter the pebble. Tonight it shines like a lighthouse.

6
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:15,900
The fireflies see the light and come back. The road of light joins up again.

7
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:18,300
There was one more lost boat. It follows the light too.

8
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:21,100
The clouds part and the aurora appears. That's home.

9
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:23,700
Someone is standing at the end of the pier, holding the map Mochi dropped.

10
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:26,300
Three snowmen. She made one each day while she waited. The third sun rises.

11
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:28,700
A whale-tail slide. The fastest way off a ship.

12
00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:31,300
One, two, three, four. Mochi hops into the empty spot.

13
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:33,900
Five. This time, no empty spot.

14
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:36,700
The scarf wraps around them both. The pebble grows warm.

15
00:00:36,900 --> 00:00:39,300
Kong brings out the parcel. The address is a drawing of a pink scarf.

16
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:41,900
Inside, a little bell. Mom ordered it so Mochi would never get lost.

17
00:00:42,100 --> 00:00:44,700
It should have arrived before the trip. Kong is sweating.

18
00:00:44,900 --> 00:00:47,300
On the same backpack where she put the pebble, she ties the bell. Jingle.

19
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:49,900
Late, but delivered after all. Mom hugs Kong too.

20
00:00:50,100 --> 00:00:52,500
That night, Mochi drew postcards. Pictures instead of words.

21
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:54,900
There's a pelican mailbox here too. The fish go along as well.

22
00:00:55,100 --> 00:00:57,300
A postcard for the conductor. And one fish.

23
00:00:57,500 --> 00:00:59,700
For the lighthouse keeper too. The fish is bigger than he is.

24
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:02,100
The crab family: the postcard on the wall, the fish on the table.

25
00:01:02,300 --> 00:01:04,700
Mu grills the fish. His face doesn't change, but his tail says it all.

26
00:01:04,900 --> 00:01:07,300
Kong has more deliveries. Mochi's bell jingles goodbye.

27
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:11,300
But there was one more parcel in Kong's cheek. It's moving. (To be continued in Season 2)

